596:			/*  #287: an all-ones exponent means the value overflowed
597:			    the DESTINATION format, and the fraction assembled
598:			    above has to go: exponent-max with a nonzero fraction
599:			    is a NaN, and mostly a SIGNALING one, where hardware
600:			    gives +/-Inf (1e300 stored as 0x7fbf21e4). #255 cannot

