8928:Example
8929:
8930:An example is shown using assembler mnemonics, indicating the states before and after execution
8931:of the instruction.
8932:
8933:Italics (e.g., .align) indicate an assembler control instruction. The meaning of the assembler
8934:control instructions is given below. For details, refer to the Cross-Assembler User's Manual.
8935:
8936:.org          Location counter setting
8937:.data.w       Word integer data allocation
8938:.data.l       Longword integer data allocation
8939:.sdata        String data allocation
8940:.align 2      2-byte boundary alignment
10745:            Double-Precision
10746:            to Single-Precision
10747:            Conversion
10748:
10749:PR Format  Summary of Operation Instruction Code  Execution
10750:                                                  States T Bit
10751:
10752:0--        --                       --            --    --
10753:
10754:1 FCNVDS DRm,FPUL (float)DRm  FPUL  1111mmm010111101 2  --
10755:
10756:Description
10757:
10758:When FPSCR.PR = 1: This instruction converts the double-precision floating-point number in
10759:DRm to a single-precision floating-point number, and stores the result in FPUL.
10760:
10761:When FPSCR.enable.O/U/I is set, an FPU exception trap is generated regardless of whether or not
10762:an exception has occurred. When an exception occurs, correct exception information is reflected in
10763:FPSCR.cause and FPSCR.flag, and FPUL is not updated. Appropriate processing should therefore
10764:be performed by software.
10765:
10766:Operation
10767:
10768:   void FCNVDS(int m, float *FPUL){
10769:            case((FPSCR.PR){
10770:                     0: undefined_operation(); /* reserved */
10771:                     1: fcnvds(m, *FPUL); break; /* FCNVDS */
10772:            }
10773:
10774:   }
10775:   void fcnvds(int m, float *FPUL)
10776:   {
10777:
10778:            pc += 2;
10779:            clear_cause();
10780:            case(data_type_of(m, *FPUL)){
10781:
10782:                     NORM :
10783:                     PZERO :
10784:                     NZERO : normal_ fcnvds(m, *FPUL); break;
10785:                     DENORM : set_E();
10786:                     PINF : *FPUL = 0x7f800000; break;
10787:                     NINF : *FPUL = 0xff800000; break;
10788:
10789:Rev. 5.0, 04/01, page 238 of 394
10790:           qNaN : *FPUL = 0x7fbfffff; break;
10791:
10792:           sNaN :     set_V();
10793:
10794:                      if((FPSCR & ENABLE_V) == 0) *FPUL = 0x7fbfffff;
10795:
10796:                      else fpu_exception_trap(); break;
10797:
10798:   }
10799:
10800:}
