The handler and decoder match the cited line numbers. Two claims need qualification: undefined casts prevent an all-input guarantee about HEAD’s DRn result, and form (g) is already caught if the FPUL rows use DR2. I also read `qnan(n)`: the manual specifies `7ff7ffff ffffffff`, which differs from the helper’s NaN encoding.
